WEBVTT

00:04.820 --> 00:06.490
Oh! Looks like she's here!

00:10.920 --> 00:12.280
Good day to you!

00:12.280 --> 00:13.380
Morning.

00:15.240 --> 00:18.990
Is this really enough to repay you?

00:18.990 --> 00:20.750
Yes. It's just what I need.

00:20.750 --> 00:23.060
Oto-chan already went on ahead.

00:23.060 --> 00:26.050
Really? Then I'll go catch up to her!

00:29.380 --> 00:32.290
Is that burned-out device a cursed object?

00:32.290 --> 00:37.390
It seems that Yorumun's water and 
Uname-sensei's fire turned it into one.

00:37.670 --> 00:42.740
Huh. Will you be able to trade it for the 
all-important ticket to your destination?

00:42.740 --> 00:44.650
That's the tricky part.

00:44.650 --> 00:50.150
Is it? I'd think that a garei 
would be pretty rare.

00:50.150 --> 00:52.460
But it might not be.

00:52.460 --> 00:59.470
Manga, anime, games, music, theater, 
movies and TV dramas, novels—

00:59.470 --> 01:02.070
works that creators whittle down 
their own lives to make...

01:02.070 --> 01:05.020
I think there are more of them 
now than there were before.

01:05.020 --> 01:10.300
They might be waiting somewhere, even now, 
for the day they are remembered.

01:10.300 --> 01:12.100
That's true.

01:12.510 --> 01:16.560
Which means the garei of my work 
must be somewhere out there, too!

01:16.910 --> 01:19.730
Write your new novel before thinking 
about stuff like that, Eyebrows.

01:19.730 --> 01:20.930
That's just mean.

01:23.170 --> 01:24.680
About that...

01:24.680 --> 01:28.050
Ever since I started getting caught up 
in all these incidents with you,

01:28.050 --> 01:30.070
my pen has been flying!

01:30.860 --> 01:34.070
Has it? This is the first I've heard of that.

01:35.220 --> 01:39.580
Remember that promise you made to read it? 
You might have to make good on that soon.

01:46.590 --> 01:51.380
<b>Mysterious Disappearances</b>

01:46.590 --> 01:51.380
<b>Mysterious Disappearances</b>

03:13.420 --> 03:18.840
<b>Cats, Swimsuits, and a Black Aeonium</b>

03:13.420 --> 03:18.840
<b>Cats, Swimsuits, and a Black Aeonium</b>

03:17.380 --> 03:20.230
Summer's right around the corner.

03:24.940 --> 03:27.080
Do you like summer?

03:27.080 --> 03:29.700
I'm quite partial to it.

03:29.700 --> 03:34.710
There's nothing better than an ice-cold beer 
after working up a sweat outdoors!

03:41.960 --> 03:44.710
Ta-da! I have an announcement!

03:44.710 --> 03:47.620
I have never once worn a swimsuit!

03:48.760 --> 03:52.380
Huh? Not once? Not even when 
you were a kid? For real?

03:52.380 --> 03:56.980
When we had swim class at school, 
I always skipped because I didn't feel well,

03:56.980 --> 04:00.720
and I've never once been to the 
beach or a pool with friends.

04:00.720 --> 04:02.720
And of course, I can't swim!

04:03.130 --> 04:07.150
You've never been to the beach 
or a pool with friends?

04:07.150 --> 04:08.640
That's just so sad.

04:09.250 --> 04:11.650
Reacting only to that part 
is against the rules.

04:12.010 --> 04:15.170
So people with no swimsuit 
experience really do exist.

04:15.170 --> 04:17.280
Of course they do. It's not that big a deal.

04:17.280 --> 04:22.030
Adashino-kun, why don't we go to 
the beach with Oto-chan one day?

04:23.960 --> 04:26.900
Of course! It would be my pleasure!

04:26.900 --> 04:31.040
In that case, I'll pick out 
your very first swimsuit.

04:31.610 --> 04:33.400
No, thank you.

04:33.830 --> 04:37.290
A cow-print or side-tie bikini would be great.

04:37.290 --> 04:41.790
Actually, a sporty one-piece 
might look even better.

04:41.790 --> 04:44.350
Now I'm getting excited!

04:53.310 --> 04:55.820
I won't be wearing any of those. Understand?

04:55.820 --> 04:58.830
No, I'll be sure to choose one that suits you.

04:58.830 --> 05:01.400
I haven't any ulterior motives at all.

05:06.580 --> 05:10.830
Huh? You're the cat that 
paid me a visit, aren't you?

05:22.340 --> 05:24.090
<b>Number Withheld</b>

05:24.810 --> 05:27.350
Hello? Is that you, old man?

05:27.350 --> 05:31.540
<i>I'm telling you this just in case. 
A cat will be coming your way.</i>

05:32.230 --> 05:35.510
<i>She may look like a young girl, 
but don't underestimate her.</i>

05:35.510 --> 05:37.100
<i>She means to kill you.</i>

05:38.090 --> 05:38.860
Huh?

05:41.750 --> 05:45.290
There's someone on top of the 
bridge pylon! It looks like a girl!

05:45.290 --> 05:46.740
A girl?

05:49.240 --> 05:51.400
My eyes aren't playing tricks on me, right?

05:54.850 --> 05:56.000
Cat ears?

06:01.620 --> 06:04.760
Nice to meet you, Disappearances-kun.

06:05.140 --> 06:06.010
Who are you?

06:06.290 --> 06:10.520
I'm the one who manages 
the Curiosities around here.

06:11.370 --> 06:14.270
You may call me the Cat Sovereign.

06:14.270 --> 06:15.970
Come on, now...

06:25.610 --> 06:26.870
Adashino-kun!

06:30.870 --> 06:33.260
I'll be taking this, meow.

06:36.500 --> 06:40.500
You always take the Curiosities somewhere 
and do away with 'em, right?

06:40.500 --> 06:43.630
I can't have that. Stop it, okay?

06:43.630 --> 06:46.390
Or if you prefer... You can die.

06:55.740 --> 06:56.900
Stop this!

06:56.900 --> 06:58.830
So you're the Bearer of Youth?

06:58.830 --> 07:00.410
Don't interfere, meow!

07:00.410 --> 07:01.400
What about you?

07:01.780 --> 07:04.400
What do you have against Adashino-kun?

07:04.400 --> 07:07.170
All he does is get in my way.

07:07.170 --> 07:08.660
What <i>don't</i> I have against him?

07:08.660 --> 07:11.410
But starting a fight out 
of nowhere isn't right!

07:14.160 --> 07:16.660
Knock that Bearer of Youth down 
until she can't get up again!

07:17.920 --> 07:20.240
Huh? What is it?

07:29.790 --> 07:33.660
What? You owe the Bearer of Youth a debt 
of gratitude for a night's food and rest,

07:33.660 --> 07:35.730
so you don't want to bully her?

07:37.070 --> 07:40.690
Tch! I guess we'll leave it at that for today.

07:47.390 --> 07:48.450
Hello?

07:48.450 --> 07:52.440
<i>It seems she's something like the boss 
of the Curiosities in that area.</i>

07:52.860 --> 07:56.560
<i>She hates you, but you can 
just leave her alone for now.</i>

07:56.560 --> 07:59.390
Seriously, where is he watching from?

08:01.270 --> 08:02.210
Here.

08:03.510 --> 08:04.960
Thank you.

08:04.960 --> 08:07.120
It's important to you, right?

08:07.120 --> 08:09.970
I'm sorry for being so weak.

08:18.120 --> 08:20.980
Well, here's where we part ways for today.

08:20.980 --> 08:23.980
Okay. I hope you can get the ticket you need.

08:23.980 --> 08:25.250
Me, too.

08:25.250 --> 08:27.120
You seem a little down.

08:27.440 --> 08:31.090
Only because you won't let me 
pick out a swimsuit for you.

08:31.090 --> 08:34.000
When you ask the impossible, 
don't be disappointed with the answer.

08:34.530 --> 08:36.270
I'll see you tomorrow at the bookstore.

08:36.270 --> 08:37.130
Right.

08:47.950 --> 08:53.100
How did Yorumun become self-aware? 
And how many meters long was she?

09:04.410 --> 09:05.610
Surprise.

09:08.610 --> 09:10.740
<b>KISARAGI</b>

09:15.740 --> 09:20.880
<i>My, my! An electronic device 
with a garei sealed inside.</i>

09:20.880 --> 09:23.570
<i>There has been a slight 
increase in those lately.</i>

09:23.570 --> 09:24.960
<i>Will this do?</i>

09:24.960 --> 09:31.260
<i>It seems that the Curiosity's data hasn't 
been saved within this cursed object.</i>

09:31.920 --> 09:35.310
<i>I'd say it would be best 
not to get your hopes up.</i>

09:35.730 --> 09:37.050
<i>I see.</i>

09:37.050 --> 09:39.270
<i>However, if by chance...</i>

09:56.020 --> 09:57.120
Ren-nii!

10:20.680 --> 10:22.060
Strike!

10:32.610 --> 10:36.110
Really? You won't be around 
during summer vacation?

10:36.110 --> 10:39.420
No, so I won't be able to 
come here. I'm very sorry.

10:39.420 --> 10:42.960
You're wearing the clothes I bought you.

10:42.960 --> 10:43.620
Yes.

10:43.620 --> 10:45.870
That's enough to make me happy.

10:48.640 --> 10:50.120
Meow!

11:12.520 --> 11:13.670
Is something wrong?

11:13.670 --> 11:16.280
I was wondering if it'd be all right 
for me to stay over again.

11:16.280 --> 11:18.280
I see.

11:20.780 --> 11:24.560
So, how'd it go? Did everything 
with the ticket work out?

11:24.970 --> 11:27.010
It seems we'll be able to go home.

11:27.010 --> 11:29.540
Really? Is that really true?

11:29.900 --> 11:30.820
Yes.

11:30.820 --> 11:32.270
At long last?

11:32.270 --> 11:33.300
That's right.

11:33.300 --> 11:35.930
That's great, Oto-chan!

11:35.930 --> 11:38.080
So you can go back where you're from, right?

11:38.480 --> 11:39.460
Yes.

11:40.680 --> 11:43.980
Oh. The black aeonium bloomed.

11:44.680 --> 11:46.130
I'm glad.

11:46.620 --> 11:48.410
Are you hungry?

11:48.410 --> 11:52.070
Sorry. I don't really eat while I'm writing.

11:52.070 --> 11:53.800
I brought food.

11:53.800 --> 11:57.560
You're a lifesaver! 
I'll take a little break, then.

12:01.930 --> 12:03.820
When will you be leaving?

12:03.820 --> 12:08.780
Ren-nii is saying it'll be after 
he reads your new novel.

12:08.780 --> 12:12.710
Really? You might make it 
home really soon, then.

12:12.710 --> 12:13.960
What?

12:14.470 --> 12:16.910
I think it's just about finished.

12:17.720 --> 12:20.610
And if that's the case, 
I'll have to work my hardest!

12:23.940 --> 12:25.550
I see.

12:27.630 --> 12:31.010
Really? So she'll be finished 
writing soon, then.

12:31.010 --> 12:32.340
<i>That's what she said.</i>

12:32.340 --> 12:35.600
All right. Your summer vacation 
starts tomorrow, right?

12:35.600 --> 12:36.490
<i>Yes.</i>

12:36.970 --> 12:40.370
You should relax and rest at 
Sumireko-san's place tonight.

12:41.430 --> 12:44.110
<i>Ren-nii, goodnight.</i>

12:44.110 --> 12:44.990
Goodnight.

12:51.920 --> 12:54.680
What's your new novel about?

12:55.420 --> 13:00.980
Basically, it's about all the different 
Curiosities I've seen since I met you two.

13:00.980 --> 13:05.680
Of course, since it's a novel, 
I've changed people's names and stuff.

13:06.780 --> 13:08.270
Is that even interesting?

13:08.270 --> 13:10.890
Don't be rude.

13:10.890 --> 13:13.270
This story is about Adashino-kun and you.

13:13.270 --> 13:16.370
How could it not be interesting?

13:17.130 --> 13:19.050
I guess that's all right, then.

13:19.050 --> 13:21.130
Does your summer vacation start soon?

13:21.130 --> 13:26.030
Yep, tomorrow. I'm going 
to the pool at Nodoka's place.

13:26.030 --> 13:29.540
Really? Then your swimsuit 
is in that backpack?

13:29.540 --> 13:31.150
Yeah...

13:31.150 --> 13:34.280
What kind of swimsuit? Is it a cute one?

13:34.280 --> 13:35.880
Will you show me?

13:35.880 --> 13:37.550
I don't know...

13:37.550 --> 13:42.330
If you want to see it, you should just 
come to the pool with us tomorrow.

13:42.330 --> 13:46.940
Unfortunately, I don't have 
a swimsuit of my own.

13:46.940 --> 13:47.930
What?

13:48.700 --> 13:50.500
It's something my grandmother told me.

13:50.870 --> 13:54.560
She said that if I got close to the ocean 
or a pool, a curse awaited me.

13:55.020 --> 13:57.320
What? What kind of curse?

13:57.320 --> 14:01.210
Um, well... A kappa's, of course.

14:01.210 --> 14:02.320
A kappa's?

14:02.320 --> 14:03.410
That's right.

14:03.410 --> 14:08.660
A long time ago, my grandfather saw 
the corpse of a kappa by the Tama River.

14:08.660 --> 14:09.700
That's what she told me.

14:09.700 --> 14:13.460
So basically, you're scared of water, right?

14:17.730 --> 14:21.070
Oto-chan, what's it like where you're from?

14:21.070 --> 14:24.920
It's just normal, I think. 
It's where I was born.

14:24.920 --> 14:26.310
Is it a nice place?

14:26.310 --> 14:28.240
It is. Probably.

14:28.240 --> 14:29.850
What's that supposed to mean?

14:30.720 --> 14:34.100
I'm sure everyone's waiting for me.

14:34.100 --> 14:36.030
And for Adashino-kun, too?

14:42.110 --> 14:43.280
Oto-chan?

14:49.630 --> 14:51.150
She fell asleep.

15:04.540 --> 15:07.040
I'm going out.

15:07.040 --> 15:09.640
Okay. Be safe.

15:28.160 --> 15:30.660
It's a private pool!

15:34.160 --> 15:37.170
<b>Adashino</b>

15:51.680 --> 15:55.240
Occhan, sorry for making you 
worry about me so much.

15:55.240 --> 15:56.840
Thanks for everything.

15:56.840 --> 15:58.760
I'm glad you're feeling better.

15:58.760 --> 16:02.230
Let's stay friends forever, okay?

16:02.230 --> 16:03.120
Yeah.

16:03.690 --> 16:06.780
<i>My! Are those two starting 
something without us?</i>

16:06.780 --> 16:08.810
<i>Oh, how scandalous. How scandalous!</i>

16:16.710 --> 16:17.900
Say...

16:17.900 --> 16:19.210
What is it?

16:19.210 --> 16:22.530
Are friends still friends 
even if they're apart?

16:22.530 --> 16:24.340
Of course they are!

16:24.340 --> 16:28.310
Even if one's on Earth and one's 
on Mars, friends are still friends!

16:28.860 --> 16:31.340
I thought so. I'm so glad!

16:32.230 --> 16:33.030
What?

16:33.350 --> 16:36.020
Adashino-kun is taking today off?

16:36.020 --> 16:37.600
He called in.

16:37.930 --> 16:42.120
He said he's so incredibly constipated 
that his whole body is stuffed full of poop.

16:42.120 --> 16:45.040
Apparently, he's holed up 
in the bathroom, crying.

16:45.420 --> 16:46.610
Yeah, no way.

16:46.930 --> 16:51.610
I never thought Adashino-kun would end up 
suffering such horrifying constipation, too.

16:51.610 --> 16:52.800
"Too"?

16:52.800 --> 16:55.950
Well, you were the same, 
weren't you, Ogawa-san?

16:55.950 --> 17:00.120
When you took that time off before, 
Adashino-kun told me all about it.

17:01.540 --> 17:03.630
That little...

17:09.190 --> 17:10.650
Um, everyone?

17:10.650 --> 17:14.890
For summer vacation, Ren-nii and I 
are going back to visit our hometown.

17:14.890 --> 17:18.390
So I'll be saying goodbye for a little while.

17:18.390 --> 17:20.390
Will you accept these?

17:20.390 --> 17:21.860
Nodoka, here.

17:21.860 --> 17:22.900
Thanks!

17:22.900 --> 17:24.340
Here, Erika.

17:24.340 --> 17:25.400
Thank you.

17:25.400 --> 17:27.010
Here, Tama-chan.

17:27.010 --> 17:28.150
Accepted with pleasure!

17:28.150 --> 17:29.580
Here, Mari.

17:29.580 --> 17:30.650
Occhan...

17:30.650 --> 17:31.950
And now...

17:37.350 --> 17:39.600
Nodoka is as bold as always.

17:39.600 --> 17:42.390
You know, Nodoka, once you become an idol,

17:42.390 --> 17:44.670
you'll have to be careful 
of sneak photographers.

17:44.670 --> 17:46.470
I'll be just fine!

17:46.920 --> 17:49.420
<b>KISARAGI</b>

17:52.430 --> 17:58.430
<i>It seems that the Curiosity's data hasn't 
been saved within this cursed object.</i>

17:58.430 --> 18:01.610
<i>I'd say it would be best 
not to get your hopes up.</i>

18:01.610 --> 18:02.910
<i>I see.</i>

18:02.910 --> 18:04.440
<i>However, if by chance...</i>

18:04.940 --> 18:09.450
<i>you were to become a ticket yourself, 
that would be a different story.</i>

18:09.450 --> 18:11.950
<i>If I became a ticket, what would happen?</i>

18:11.950 --> 18:16.040
<i>You'd become energy 
for the train, of course,</i>

18:16.040 --> 18:19.900
<i>and I imagine you'd disappear after that.</i>

18:22.450 --> 18:23.480
I'm home.

18:23.480 --> 18:24.710
Welcome back.

18:28.200 --> 18:31.460
I went and said goodbye to 
Nodoka and the others, too.

18:31.840 --> 18:33.790
It made me feel sad, though.

18:34.860 --> 18:35.960
I see.

18:37.320 --> 18:39.860
Ren-nii, did something happen?

18:39.860 --> 18:42.980
Oto, there's something 
I want to talk to you about.

18:42.980 --> 18:43.940
Huh?

18:54.730 --> 18:55.740
<b>The End</b>

18:59.120 --> 19:01.490
I hear you're constipated? Text me back
ASAP, even if your butt's glued to the can

19:08.000 --> 19:11.000
<b>KISARAGI</b>

19:29.910 --> 19:31.840
Cheers!

19:41.730 --> 19:43.540
Oto-chan?

19:44.120 --> 19:48.900
There's something I want to tell you two. 
You see, I've finished my new novel!

19:50.840 --> 19:55.800
The people at the publisher are still checking it, 
but I think it'll probably move forward.

19:55.800 --> 19:58.420
Could you tell Adashino-kun for me?

20:00.630 --> 20:05.480
Oh, you aren't with him right now? 
Then can you give him a message later?

20:05.480 --> 20:07.320
Tell him he can come and read it anytime.

20:08.170 --> 20:12.410
Yeah. And if you're still out and about, 
take care on your way back.

20:13.730 --> 20:14.870
Bye!

20:17.490 --> 20:20.950
Good news. The author Ogawa Sumireko's
new work has been completed

20:46.720 --> 20:49.730
<b>Mysterious Disappearances
Ogawa Sumireko</b>

21:02.490 --> 21:07.240
Hey, you haven't forgotten your promise, have you?
If you don't text back, I'll drink a thousand cans of coffee

21:07.240 --> 21:11.750
Hey, you haven't forgotten your promise, have you?
If you don't text back, I'll drink a thousand cans of coffee

21:07.250 --> 21:11.750
I mean, you'll owe me a thousand cans of coffee

21:24.530 --> 21:28.270
<i>Then I offer myself up as a ticket.</i>

21:28.270 --> 21:29.260
<b>Ticket Counter</b>

21:28.270 --> 21:30.990
<i>My, my. Are you certain?</i>

21:30.990 --> 21:32.430
<i>How far will she be able to go?</i>

21:32.430 --> 21:37.530
<i>With you as her ticket, your little sister 
will definitely reach the final stop:</i>

21:37.530 --> 21:40.940
<i>Andoro Station.</i>

21:39.060 --> 21:41.980
<b>Andoro Station</b>

21:40.940 --> 21:42.030
<i>If you would, please.</i>

21:42.340 --> 21:46.320
<i>Well, you are on the brink of 
destruction anyway, aren't you?</i>

23:32.620 --> 23:34.180
Delicious!

23:34.980 --> 23:39.980
<b>A Ticket, a Video, and Mysterious Disappearances</b>

23:36.090 --> 23:39.940
Next time: "A Ticket, a Video, 
and Mysterious Disappearances."
